# Ciudad Cenit, north half (C6, contract 49), 34 x 16. column = i, row = j. The city is TWO maps (one Cenit does not fit the heap budget: the three new buildings alone are 4.4 KB): this is the
# NORTH half (`ciudad_cenit`: the NORTH gate (16..17,0) from Ruta 5, the Torre Vertice, the Centro, the tienda, the fortune-teller's house); the south half (`ciudad_cenit_sur`: the Fighting dojo, the psychic gym, the mime
# trader's house, the EAST gate from Ruta 8 and the SOUTH gate from Ruta 6) is joined to it by the gap (16..17,15) of the south rail. A guard at each route lets the hero in once somebody gave him a drink: flag 837.
# Look (the user's mock "Ciudad Cenit", tools/c6_mock.py): the psychic / cyberpunk city: BIG pale slabs with a faint concentric-ring inlay (`ring_<i%2><j%2>`, never small tiles), glass TOWERS (back sides: north and west
# edges), low glass rails (front sides: south and east), floating ORBS on stands (animated) and street lamps. The Torre Vertice (door (15,6)), the Centro (door (25,4), the Planeador lands in front of it:
# @fly slot 8), the tienda (door (29,4)), the fortune-teller's house (door (7,4): the fortune-teller, Disc 08). Three Team Vertice grunts (static art: they slide up to the hero) hold the streets until Varo falls (flag 852).
@map ciudad_cenit
@size 34 16
@interior no
@area ciudad_cenit
@fly 8 ciudad_cenit 25 5 face=S   # the Planeador lands here, in front of the Centro door; slot 8 = visited flag 992 (contract 46.1)
@flag varo_vtx 852   # Director Varo was beaten in the Torre Vertice: the street grunts are gone
@bg 0
@fill ring_00
@spawn north 16 1 S
@spawn south 16 14 N
@spawn centro_door 25 5 S
@spawn tienda_door 29 5 S
@spawn torre_door 15 7 S
@spawn psi_door 7 5 S
